 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>A <b>Statement</b> object is used to send SQL commands to the database through a Connection.</p><h3>Execute methods</h3><ul><li><b>executeQuery(sql)</b>: SELECT → returns ResultSet.</li><li><b>executeUpdate(sql)</b>: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL → returns int (rows affected).</li><li><b>execute(sql)</b>: any SQL → returns boolean.</li></ul><table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Use</th><th>Created by</th></tr><tr><td>Statement</td><td>Fixed SQL, no parameters</td><td>con.createStatement()</td></tr><tr><td>PreparedStatement</td><td>SQL with ? parameters, precompiled, prevents SQL injection</td><td>con.prepareStatement(sql)</td></tr><tr><td>CallableStatement</td><td>Call stored procedures</td><td>con.prepareCall(\"{call p(?)}\")</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which statement uses ? placeholders and prevents SQL injection?",
  "options": [
   "Statement",
   "PreparedStatement",
   "ResultSet"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Simple People Call: P = Prepared."
 }
